{"ts": 1784364926.111353, "event": "finish", "summary": "Held the entire episode. The short entry was correct from the start: price moved favorably almost immediately, dipped briefly near breakeven around t=4m but recovered, then ran to a peak of about +195pts by t=22m before giving back roughly half into the close (still +68pts favorable at window end). No frame showed a genuine wrong-direction reversal -- the pullbacks were gradual profit-taking/retracement against an already-large winning move, not a directional flip against the thesis, so there was never a bail signal. Next time I'd watch for a faster, steeper retracement slope (not just cumulative giveback %) plus multiple against-fires clustering in the same direction as a real wrong-direction tell, since the persistent single-frame giveback here never accelerated into that pattern.", "exit_frame": null, "n_commits": 33}
